by URL with any trailing slash ignored. A value that is neither, such as
\code{RSPM}, is matched to the lockfile's only Package Manager repository when
there is exactly one. Pins that match no repository are not compared.
\item On glibc Linux, with boosterpak's repository setup enabled (see
\code{BOOSTERPAK_CONFIGURE_REPOSITORIES}), each generic Package Manager URL is
checked as the Linux binary URL a restore on this machine would use, such
as \verb{<host>/cran/__linux__/manylinux_2_28/latest}. Otherwise the URL as
recorded is checked, because that is what a restore uses. Distro URLs such
as \verb{<host>/cran/__linux__/noble/latest} are checked as they are.
